{
  "id": "lesson-ef-037",
  "slug": "entity-framework-core-with-existing-database",
  "moduleSlug": "database-first-diagnostics",
  "title": "EF Core with Existing Database",
  "description": "Learn Database-First approach using Scaffold-DbContext for reverse engineering.",
  "order": 1,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 28,
  "tags": ["ef-core", "database-first", "scaffold-dbcontext", "reverse-engineering"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The **Database-First approach** creates entity and context classes from an existing database using the `Scaffold-DbContext` command (reverse engineering)."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Scaffold-DbContext Command"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Scaffold Command",
        "content": "Reverse engineering existing database",
        "language": "powershell",
        "code": "Scaffold-DbContext \"Server=.\\SQLExpress;Database=SchoolDB;Trusted_Connection=True;\" Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer -OutputDir Models"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Parameters"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Parameter", "Description"],
        "rows": [
          ["Connection", "Database connection string"],
          ["Provider", "EF Core provider (e.g., SqlServer)"],
          ["OutputDir", "Directory for generated classes"],
          ["Context", "Name of DbContext class"],
          ["Schemas", "Schemas to include"],
          ["Tables", "Tables to scaffold"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Generated Classes"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "The command creates:"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Entity classes for each table",
          "DbContext class with Fluent API configurations",
          "OnConfiguring method with connection string"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "DotNet CLI Equivalent"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "CLI Scaffold Command",
        "content": "Using dotnet ef dbcontext scaffold",
        "language": "bash",
        "code": "dotnet ef dbcontext scaffold \"Server=.\\SQLEXPRESS;Database=SchoolDB;Trusted_Connection=True;\" Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer -o Models"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "data": {
        "variant": "info",
        "title": "Note",
        "text": "EF Core creates entity classes only for tables, not for stored procedures or views. Use migrations after scaffolding to keep database up to date."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "summary-box",
      "data": {
        "title": "Key Takeaways",
        "points": [
          "Database-First uses Scaffold-DbContext",
          "Creates entity and context classes",
          "Supports PMC and CLI commands",
          "Use migrations after scaffolding for updates"
        ],
        "takeaway": "Continue to learn about logging."
      }
    }
  ],
